  "body": "Follow-up to #131 / PR #162. This adds machine files for the other Tormach mills whose operator's manuals were available, and lets each machine file state the two spindle facts the PathPilot post had hard-coded for the 770 family.\n\n### Machines\nEach file uses its own Tormach operator's manual (public Tormach documentation, § Machine Specifications / Performance Expectations). All are inch machines with Flood M8 and Mist M7 (every manual documents M07/M08/M09). Travel is ± the full stroke in program coordinates, as on the 770MX.\n\n| Machine (Setup pane) | Manual | Travel X/Y/Z in | rpm | belt ranges | kW | XY/Z IPM | rigid tap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Tormach 770MX *(existing, MF serials)* | UM10587 | 14 / 7.5 / 13.25 | 175–10000 | 175–3250, 525–10000 | 1.1 | 300 / 250 | yes |\n| Tormach 770MX (ML) | UM10864 | 14 / 7.5 / 13.25 | 250–10000 | one | 1.5 | 450 / 420 | yes |\n| Tormach 770M | UM10539 | 14 / 7.5 / 13.25 | 175–10000 | 175–3250, 525–10000 | 1.1 | 135 / 110 | **no** (R8) |\n| Tormach 1100MX | UM10586 | 18 / 11 / 16.25 | 70–10000 | 70–2000, 250–10000 | 1.5 | 300 / 230 | yes |\n| Tormach 1500MX | UM10811 | 19.7 / 13.8 / 14 | 250–10000 | one | 3.0 | 1200 / 600 | yes |\n| Tormach PCNC 440 | UM10372 | 10 / 6.25 / 10 | 300–10000 | 300–4500, 650–10000 | 0.56 | 135 / 110 | **no** (R8) |\n\nThe ML-serial 770MX (EtherCAT) has a different spindle from the MF one, so it is its own entry.\n\n**Not included:** the non-MX 1100 and the plain 770, because neither manual was available. That is why this PR says **Refs** #170: the issue stays open for those two.\n\n### `.mch` additions (both optional; unstated = today's behaviour)\n- `spindle.ranges: [{min_speed, max_speed}, ...]` → `machine.spindleRanges`. The Tormach post's belt note now uses the machine's own ranges, not the 770's hard-coded numbers. A machine with fewer than two ranges gets no note.\n- `spindle.rigid_tapping: false` → `machine.rigidTapping`. On such a machine the Tormach post refuses a tap cycle by name (one counted warning, which blocks the post) and never writes `G84`.\n\nGolden change: `synth_tormach.nc` (posted against the generic metric VMC, which states no ranges) loses its 770-family belt comment. The 770MX goldens are unchanged.\n\nThe decisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/170-tormach-machines.md`.\n\n### Tests\nNew: `crates/app/tests/tormach_machines.rs`:\n- `every_tormach_machine_states_its_manuals_figures`\n- `the_script_sees_the_ranges_and_the_tapping_word`\n- `the_belt_note_follows_the_machines_own_ranges` (for example, 2500 rpm names HIGH on the 1100MX and nothing on the 770MX)\n- `a_rigid_tap_is_refused_on_a_machine_that_cannot_rigid_tap`\n\n`machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` now lists the new entries.\n\nQuick gate on the final tip (rebased on main at f4e4eac): post, sim, geometry, cl and tools ok; clippy ok. The failures are the same as on `main` without this PR:\n- `drilling_cross_box` / `drilling_cross_spindle` (#151)\n- `swarf_pose_continuity`\n- `headless_run_succeeds` and the window tests (headless GPU on this Mac)\n- `tool_editor_snapshot`: fails on current `main`, because #178's new `PRB-0400` catalog tool lengthens the catalog list and the scrollbar thumb shrinks (20 px). That is a stale snapshot, unrelated to this PR.\n\n### Still to do before ready (draft until then)\n- PathPilot Hub simulation of a program posted for the 1100MX and the 770M (belt note, and the tap refusal on the 770M).\n- GUI check that the new machines appear in the Setup pane's machine list.\n\nChangelog: Machine files for the Tormach 770MX (ML), 770M, 1100MX, 1500MX and PCNC 440; a .mch can state its spindle belt ranges and whether it can rigid-tap, and the Tormach post names the machine's own belt range and refuses G84 on a machine that cannot rigid-tap (#170, PR #M)\n\nRefs #170\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
